WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.403 --> 00:00:03.110
- [Narrator] Thora Birch is an actress.

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:06.079
She's been in a lot of movies.

00:00:06.079 --> 00:00:07.273
Like ...

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.412
a lot of movies.

00:00:09.412 --> 00:00:11.765
- I'm trying to find myself.

00:00:11.765 --> 00:00:14.738
- [Narrator] Let's settle
in and listen to a few tales

00:00:14.738 --> 00:00:17.510
from some of Thora's most iconic films.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:20.096
- So whatever I say, just smile and nod.

00:00:20.096 --> 00:00:23.596
(lively orchestral music)

00:00:24.652 --> 00:00:26.572
- Hi, my name is Thora
Birch, and I've been acting

00:00:26.572 --> 00:00:30.466
in film and television
since I was four years old.

00:00:30.466 --> 00:00:32.712
The beginning of the ‘90s with Hocus Pocus.

00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:35.257
I was kind of cast as the sassy blonde kid

00:00:35.257 --> 00:00:36.723
that always had something
a little bit too smart

00:00:36.723 --> 00:00:38.607
for her own age to say.

00:00:38.607 --> 00:00:40.239
- Stuff it, zit face!

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:41.712
- Well, I remember with Hocus Pocus

00:00:41.712 --> 00:00:44.134
that I was so thrilled to
have been a part of it,

00:00:44.134 --> 00:00:45.517
to have worked with Bette Midler.

00:00:45.517 --> 00:00:46.942
And I fell in love with Kathy Najimy

00:00:46.942 --> 00:00:48.984
and Sarah Jessica Parker.

00:00:48.984 --> 00:00:50.799
But it came out at an awkward time.

00:00:50.799 --> 00:00:52.781
It didn't really come
out around Halloween.

00:00:52.781 --> 00:00:54.410
(screaming)

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.702
And then, 10 years after that,

00:00:56.702 --> 00:00:59.529
people would come up to me and be
like, "Hey, wait a second,

00:00:59.529 --> 00:01:01.993
"are you Danny from Hocus Pocus?"

00:01:01.993 --> 00:01:02.937
And I'd be like, "Wait, wait, what?

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:04.788
"Hocus Pocus, what are you talking about?"

00:01:04.788 --> 00:01:06.561
And then it just like ...

00:01:06.561 --> 00:01:09.056
My awareness of it
growing into this kind of

00:01:09.056 --> 00:01:11.013
cult-like thing, I was
like, "Oh, okay, wow.

00:01:11.013 --> 00:01:12.930
"It's got a long life."

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:15.845
What I loved about Now &amp; Then

00:01:15.845 --> 00:01:20.270
was it was about friendships
and how important they are.

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:22.062
It's a coming-of-age movie.

00:01:22.062 --> 00:01:24.065
And also, we had a female writer,

00:01:24.065 --> 00:01:27.145
we had a female director,
female producers.

00:01:27.145 --> 00:01:30.145
It was very much female empowerment.

00:01:31.138 --> 00:01:34.053
For a group of 12-year-old
girls to be working

00:01:34.053 --> 00:01:36.013
on a film like that, I didn't even realize

00:01:36.013 --> 00:01:38.763
how important it was at the time.

00:01:40.817 --> 00:01:42.587
American Beauty, I would love to say

00:01:42.587 --> 00:01:44.923
that I didn't relate to Jane
in any way, shape or form,

00:01:44.923 --> 00:01:48.781
and that I was so much more
fun-loving than she was,

00:01:48.781 --> 00:01:51.948
but no, there was a soulful connection

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:54.338
to her malaise.

00:01:54.338 --> 00:01:57.813
But what I did also respond
to specifically was that,

00:01:57.813 --> 00:02:00.081
through the course of the
film, she herself changed.

00:02:00.081 --> 00:02:01.456
The Jane at the end of
the film is very different

00:02:01.456 --> 00:02:03.846
from the Jane that we first
meet at the beginning.

00:02:03.846 --> 00:02:07.054
Well, for me the beginning
of the ‘90s with Hocus Pocus,

00:02:07.054 --> 00:02:09.549
to the end of the 90s,
shooting American Beauty,

00:02:09.549 --> 00:02:12.097
it was almost like being
in a different decade.

00:02:12.097 --> 00:02:14.809
Things had changed that much,

00:02:14.809 --> 00:02:18.226
but also I grew up and changed that much.

00:02:20.065 --> 00:02:22.492
Having done this since the
age of like four-and-a-half,

00:02:22.492 --> 00:02:25.814
I've learned different
things from different shoots.

00:02:25.814 --> 00:02:28.764
It's not so much about
waiting for one experience

00:02:28.764 --> 00:02:31.313
that's gonna be like a
career-defining thing.

00:02:31.313 --> 00:02:33.549
I think it's just enjoying the moment

00:02:33.549 --> 00:02:35.981
and what you're presented with today.

00:02:35.981 --> 00:02:38.814
(climactic music)

